We are focusing on the space of Eisenstein Series that arise from the right action of $GL(n,\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$ on $I(n)$. This space is part of the Langlands Classification, and we're specifically looking at the $P_{4,m}$-spaces, which are subspaces of $I(4,\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$. This investigation is a continuation of the work begun by A. Alevy Lagneau in "Poles of Eisenstein Series from the Symmetric Power $S_{2n-2}(\pi_\infty \otimes \psi_2)$". 

Our goal is to determine the partial L-function for an Eisenstein Series, $E_{2n-2}(\psi_2,f)$. This is a continuation of Lagneau's work which found a novel method for calculating the partial L-function. We find that this can be done by summing the local Whittaker functions of the unramified right action of $GL(2,\mathbb{A}_\mathbb{Q})$. 

